          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: அரசவை",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அரசவை — aracavai — \"a royal court\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "புலவர் அரசவையில் ஒரு பாடல் பாடினார். pulavar aracavaiyil oru pāṭal pāṭiṉār. The poet sang a song at the royal court."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அரசு, king + அவை, assembly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அரசவை (aracavai) joins அரசு, \"king, kingdom\", which DEDR 201 traces to Sanskrit rājan, with அவை, \"assembly\", usually traced to Sanskrit sabhā, \"assembly, hall\" (CDIAL 13167)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
