          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மகுடம் — makuṭam — \"a crown\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மன்னரின் மகுடத்தில் பல வைரங்கள் இருந்தன. maṉṉariṉ makuṭattil pala vairaṅkaḷ iruntaṉa. There were many diamonds in the king's crown."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also a crowning glory: வெற்றியின் மகுடம் (makuṭam)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மகுடம் (makuṭam) is borrowed from Sanskrit mukuṭa, makuṭa, \"tiara, crest\" (CDIAL 10144); CDIAL notes that the Sanskrit word may itself come from a Dravidian word for \"top\"."
            }
          ]
        },
